      "options": {
        "code": { "language": "plaintext", "showLineNumbers": false, "showMiniMap": false },
        "content": "## Setup\n\nSet these four dashboard variables before anything renders:\n\n- `metric_started`, `metric_error`, `metric_completed` — Klaviyo metric **IDs**, not names. Get them with `scripts/list-metrics.sh`.\n- `event_source` — the `source` property your app sends, e.g. `website`.\n\nA metric does not exist until its first event fires, so run one real journey first.\n\n## How to read this\n\n**Error rate** and **completion rate** are computed across the whole window in the source query. **Affected users** counts distinct profiles with at least one error — that is the list worth acting on.\n\nDrill into a specific failure by querying Get Events for the `session_id` of an affected profile.\n\n## Limits\n\n- Reads the newest **1,000 events** per window with no truncation warning. Long windows silently under-count.\n- Stage ratios are **aggregate comparisons, not ordered funnels**. A user counted in Completed did not necessarily appear in Attempts within this window.\n- Refresh is 30s polling plus Klaviyo processing delay.\n- No session replay, stack traces, or error grouping.\n\n## Adding panels\n\nPoint new panels at source panel **50** or **51** via the `-- Dashboard --` data source. Do not add a new upstream query per panel — concurrent aggregate queries return HTTP 429.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "How to read this",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": { "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource", "uid": "klaviyo-api" },
      "description": "Shared source query. One Klaviyo API call feeding every rollup panel above. Aggregation happens in JSONata because Query Metric Aggregates cannot group by arbitrary event properties.",
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": {}, "overrides": [] },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 18 },
      "id": 50,
      "options": {
        "cellHeight": "sm",
        "footer": { "countRows": false, "fields": "", "reducer": ["sum"], "show": false },
        "showHeader": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": { "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource", "uid": "klaviyo-api" },
          "filters": [],
          "format": "table",
          "global_query_id": "",
          "parser": "backend",
          "refId": "A",
          "root_selector": "( $mStart := \"${metric_started}\"; $mError := \"${metric_error}\"; $mDone := \"${metric_completed}\"; $src := \"${event_source}\"; $events := data[(relationships.metric.data.id = $mStart or relationships.metric.data.id = $mError or relationships.metric.data.id = $mDone) and attributes.event_properties.source = $src]; $count($events) = 0 ? [] : ( $starts := $events[relationships.metric.data.id = $mStart]; $errors := $events[relationships.metric.data.id = $mError]; $dones := $events[relationships.metric.data.id = $mDone]; $errorRate := $count($starts) = 0 ? 0 : $count($errors) / $count($starts); $completionRate := $count($starts) = 0 ? 0 : $count($dones) / $count($starts); $affected := $count($distinct($errors.relationships.profile.data.id)); $latencies := $errors.attributes.event_properties.latency_ms; $avgLatency := $count($latencies) = 0 ? 0 : $average($latencies); $days := $sort([$distinct($map($events, function($e) { $substring($e.attributes.datetime, 0, 10) }))]); [$map($days, function($d) {( $day := $events[$substring(attributes.datetime, 0, 10) = $d]; { \"day\": $d, \"attempts\": $count($day[relationships.metric.data.id = $mStart]), \"errors\": $count($day[relationships.metric.data.id = $mError]), \"completed\": $count($day[relationships.metric.data.id = $mDone]), \"affected_users\": $affected, \"overall_error_rate\": $errorRate, \"overall_completion_rate\": $completionRate, \"avg_latency_ms\": $avgLatency } )})] ) )",
          "source": "url",
          "type": "json",
          "url": "https://a.klaviyo.com/api/events/?filter=and(greater-or-equal(datetime,${__from:date:iso}),less-than(datetime,${__to:date:iso}))&page%5Bsize%5D=1000&sort=-datetime",
          "url_options": { "data": "", "method": "GET" }
        }
      ],
      "title": "Source — workflow rollup (shared)",
      "type": "table"
    },
    {
      "datasource": { "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource", "uid": "klaviyo-api" },
      "description": "Shared source query for the failure-reason distribution. Second and final upstream call per refresh.",
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": {}, "overrides": [] },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 18 },
      "id": 51,
      "options": {
        "cellHeight": "sm",
        "footer": { "countRows": false, "fields": "", "reducer": ["sum"], "show": false },
        "showHeader": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": { "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource", "uid": "klaviyo-api" },
          "filters": [],
          "format": "table",
          "global_query_id": "",
          "parser": "backend",
          "refId": "A",
          "root_selector": "( $mError := \"${metric_error}\"; $src := \"${event_source}\"; $errors := data[relationships.metric.data.id = $mError and attributes.event_properties.source = $src]; $count($errors) = 0 ? [] : ( $reasons := [$distinct($errors.attributes.event_properties.reason)]; [$map($reasons, function($r) {{ \"reason\": $r, \"count\": $count($errors[attributes.event_properties.reason = $r]) }})] ) )",
          "source": "url",
          "type": "json",
          "url": "https://a.klaviyo.com/api/events/?filter=and(greater-or-equal(datetime,${__from:date:iso}),less-than(datetime,${__to:date:iso}))&page%5Bsize%5D=1000&sort=-datetime",
          "url_options": { "data": "", "method": "GET" }
        }
      ],
      "title": "Source — failure reasons (shared)",
      "type": "table"
    }
